    {
      "text": "The Azure DevOps outegration webhook enables automatic syncing of Azure DevOps ticket updates such as Status or SLA changes to their corresponding Zscaler SecOps tickets, reducing the need for manual changes. This step is required when configuring the Azure DevOps to SecOps ticket mapping to keep the tickets in the two systems in sync. To learn more, see Configuring the Azure DevOps Outegration."
    },
    {
      "text": "See image."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Configuring the Azure DevOps Webhook",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To set up your Azure DevOps webhook:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Log in to the Azure Portal.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Go to Organization > Projects and select a project.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          18
        ],
        [
          21,
          29
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The project page appears.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Project Settings in the bottom-left corner.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          22
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The Project details page appears.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          19
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "In the left-side navigation, go to General > Service Hooks.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          35,
          42
        ],
        [
          45,
          58
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Create subscription.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 5,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          25
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The Service page appears.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          11
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Service page, select Web Hooks.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 6,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          14
        ],
        [
          28,
          37
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 7,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The Trigger page appears.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          11
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Select an event to trigger and configure filters. Select the options based on the work item that you are configuring the outegration for.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 8
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 9,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The Action page appears.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "For URL, enter https://webhook.avalor.io/integration/{avalor-account-id}/azure_DevOps.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 10,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          8
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Test.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 11,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Finish if the test is successful.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 12,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          12
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After your webhook is set up, configured triggers for field updates in your Azure DevOps outegration mapping automatically sync changes made to Azure DevOps tickets with their corresponding SecOps tickets."
    }
  ]
